  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday through Wednesday)\nIssued at 1240 PM CDT Wed Oct 28 2026\n\nShortwave trough with a tropical moisture plume will pass across\nthe region Friday night into Saturday. Corridor of higher rain\nchances will focus across the western periphery of the forecast\narea through Friday before higher rain chances spread further east\nFriday night into Saturday. Thicker cloud cover will keep\ntemperatures noticeably cooler on Friday. Rains are likely to\ntaper off from west to east across eastern OK Saturday evening and\ninto Saturday night across western AR. Instability continues to\nappear limited as this wave passes which is expected to keep\nlightning impact low through Saturday outdoor events.\n\nMild and dry weather is expected on Sunday ahead of the next storm\nsystem which will impact the region next Monday into Tuesday.\nEnsemble solutions remain in good agreement that a strong wave\nwill deepen across the central and southern Plains on Monday and\nthen likely make slow eastward progress through at least Tuesday.\nWidespread precip shield within the warm advection plume and along\nthe advancing cold front are likely to impact the local region. \nTiming remains varied as well as details on the warm sector \nexpansion ahead of the front and associated storm impact \npotential. Despite the uncertainties, the trend remains for \nimpactful weather early next week and updated forecasts will \ncontinue to refine details.",
